WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.478
Follow a cache hit and a cache miss through a proxy.

00:00:03.478 --> 00:00:06.220
On a hit, saved data avoids backend work.

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:10.902
On a miss, the backend supplies the value and the
cache may retain it.

00:00:10.902 --> 00:00:17.323
Use a small LRU trace to make eviction concrete,
then compare application-managed caching with a

00:00:17.323 --> 00:00:18.995
transparent intermediary.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.920
Caching exploits repeated access, especially when
popularity is uneven.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:27.524
The key design question is when reuse remains valid.

00:00:27.524 --> 00:00:33.275
Compare expiry, invalidation and versioned names,
then apply HTTP cache directives.

00:00:33.275 --> 00:00:40.066
A successful cache reduces backend work while
respecting freshness and identity boundaries; a high

00:00:40.066 --> 00:00:42.977
hit rate alone does not prove correctness.
